report={'Review':'Independent source review, not independent execution proof. No builds/tests/network/Main or Git mutation by reviewer.','Head':subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],text=True).strip(),'Blockers':[],'Files':files,'ProtectedHistoricalSources':protected,'Checks':[{'Name':'Exactly one real public MFA added','Finding':'DistributionRegistrations adds only erlang + DistributionInputNames.Function=dist_ctrl_put_data + Arity=2, delegates actual context/arguments to unchanged DistributionInputAdapter.PutData. No stub or broad new exception handler.'},{'Name':'Raw protocol gap preserved','Finding':'RawInput, UnsupportedControl and raw41 HOST/name files unchanged. Well-formed unsupported SPAWN_REQUEST29 remains NotSupportedException; no catch converts it to ok. Existing native-aligned malformed decode handling is unchanged and generation-bound.'},{'Name':'Native-backed scenario preservation','Finding':'Entire DistributionNativePayloadContractHostChecks source equals HEAD after reversing exactly Session.Put direct adapter -> runtime registered MFA call. All scenario assertions, deadlines, actor lifecycle and expected bodies unchanged.'},{'Name':'Historical compiled fixtures preserved','Finding':'Removing sole appended DistributionInputCases.Modules group yields exact HEAD source modulo checkout EOL. No other historical compiled source changes in tracked diff; OriginalOtpDefects exact same. All six exclusion declarations unchanged.'},{'Name':'Error precedence','Finding':'Cons flattened before handle validation. Handle resource checked before input-handler identity; handler mismatch notsup before data shape. RawInputAttempts increments before authorized nil/bitstring/type handling. HOST assertions distinguish invalid iolist from valid iolist unauthorized caller, wrong caller integer, valid caller integer and partial bitstring; frame asserts original Handle/Data.'},{'Name':'Meaningful nominal smoke','Finding':'Owns maps exact new MFA. Smoke adopts genuine opaque handle and explicitly assigns current controller as authorized input handler, encodes canonical SEND targeting current actor, invokes actual registry MFA, receives payload, asserts AcceptedInputPackets exactly one. No mock or fabricated handle.'},{'Name':'New compiled cases','Finding':'Current three compiled source files exactly match frozen revision2. Ten independent static badarg cases. Dynamic apply invokes exported helper through remote module dispatch and receives M/F runtime parameters. Exact [H,D]=Args before output; original atom Args preserved, ordinary reference identity validated then only ref symbolically projected. Annotations/later frames intentionally excluded.'},{'Name':'New registered HOST coverage','Finding':'Compiles guest direct/dynamic/capture module, real adopted handle and alternate input handler, binary and iolist SEND/REG_SEND with actual payload receive, nil/empty success and per-attempt counts, precedence/caller/type errors and original frame args, genuine LINK reflected in process_info links.'}],'Limitations':['New ten contracts are source-guided pending original pinned native execution; this source review is not native success proof.','No claim of whole distribution or erlang completion: unsupported controls29-37, async pressure and other recorded prerequisites remain.','Root execution results are externally reported and not re-executed or inferred here.']}
